# Global adversarial testing skill

When the user runs **`/test`**, asks to expand tests, or wants FE/BE / docs coverage:

1. Read `~/.cursor/skills/adversarial-documentation-driven-testing/SKILL.md` (symlink to the master skill).
2. If this workspace has `.cursor/commands/test.md`, follow **that** product overlay.
3. Otherwise follow `~/.cursor/commands/test.md`.
4. When `/test` reaches coverage, follow `/coverage` and loop until statement, branch, and condition are ≥ 80% on measured code, then give the user the final coverage report.
5. Rank **unverified documented behavior** above uncovered line ranges.
6. Never copy the skill into a repo as a second master; update the master and keep `~/.cursor/skills/…` symlinked to it.
